itting one run into two traces' — this is precisely the OTLP/gateway unification the epic defers.","Epic run-correlation child charter is only 'minting the per-run identity ... and populating the verdict trace_id field'; it does not authorize reading rebar's own span identity."],"finding":"The leaf derives trace_id from the active OpenTelemetry span's trace id (so the gateway header matches rebar's exported OTLP spans), which the parent epic places out of scope: the epic's 'Out of scope' bars 'unification of rebar's own OTLP spans with the gateway's records' and states the 32-hex format is chosen so 'LATER WORK can carry a real OTel trace id,' with the OTLP path 'unchanged by this epic.' The leaf steps outside the parent contract by bringing that later work into this child.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f824245b26d1d3626","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (\"trace_id ... the ACTIVE OpenTelemetry span's trace id when one is recording\") and AC line \"With a recording OpenTelemetry span active, trace_id equals that span's trace id as 32 hex\"","norm_id":"nd642f24079a4f947","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator runs with [tracing] and LANGFUSE_* set so rebar's OTLP spans export: the leaf makes the verdict/header trace_id equal the live span id, unifying the two trace sources the epic said stays split until later work."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Drop the live-span derivation: mint `secrets.token_hex(16)` unconditionally per gate run, and remove the corresponding 'with a recording span active, trace_id equals that span's trace id' acceptance criterion. This keeps the leaf a subset of the epic, whose out-of-scope section defers real-OTel-trace-id carriage to later work.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_wo